  <layout>Ornamental border at top; dedication heading in two lines, centred, italic; one column of verse, lines alternately indented; catchword "Quid!" at lower right, below the last line.</layout>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Quid!</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">Præstantissimo Domino</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="1">Authori, Contubernali Lectissimo.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">Numquid JACOBE ludimur,</l>
    <l n="4">Fortunæ volucri ludimur</l>
    <l n="5">impetu! Æternum nihil est sacro</l>
    <l n="6">Quicquid lenta tulit materies</l>
    <l n="7">sinu. Statur casibus. Occidet</l>
    <l n="8">Quod surgit, sed adhuc surget &amp; occidet,</l>
    <l n="9">Ritu præcipitis pilæ,</l>
    <l n="10">Quæ cum pulsa cava rejicitur manu,</l>
    <l n="11">Nunc leves secat Africos,</l>
    <l n="12">Nunc terræ refugis absilit ictibus:</l>
    <l n="13">Vesper vespere truditur,</l>
    <l n="14">Sed nunc deterior, nunc melior</l>
    <l n="15">subit: Magnas Fors rapit interim</l>
    <l n="16">Urbesq; &amp; populos &amp; miserabili</l>
    <l n="17">Reges subruit impetu:</l>
    <l n="18">Et sceptri decus, &amp; regna cadentium</l>
    <l n="19">Permiscet cineri Ducum;</l>
    <l n="20">Auratasq; trabes &amp; penetralia</l>
    <l n="21">Et cives simul &amp; super</l>
    <l n="22">Eversis sepelit turribus oppida.</l>
    <l n="23">Sic quod prodit in Orbem</l>
    <l n="24">Jam jam magnificè, cras miserè</l>
    <l n="25">perit; Florens hic hodie occidit,</l>
    <l n="26">Surgit mox alius natus ad aspera.</l>
    <l n="27">Eheu JACOBE ludimur,</l>
    <l n="28">Fatorum rapidâ ludimur orbitâ!</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The poem is set as a single continuous verse passage; its lines are run together here, with the printed line order kept. The printed catchword "Quid!" is given in bottom_margin. No page number or running head is printed. The ornamental border at the top is not transcribed as text.</notes>
</page>
